{
  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe underestimation bias: The model consistently forecasts a flat or slightly rising trend while true prices exhibit strong upward momentum (e.g., +15-20 EUR spikes). Apply a positive momentum adjustment of 5-10 EUR when recent history shows a sustained upward trend.",
    "Address lag in trend reversal: The model fails to anticipate the peak and subsequent decline, continuing to forecast increases after the true price has peaked (around day 15-18 in the horizon). Implement a mean-reversion trigger that reduces forecasts once the price exceeds the 20-day moving average by more than 5 EUR.",
    "Incorporate sentiment magnitude: Positive sentiment scores (0.20-0.50) correlate with immediate price surges not captured by the model. When sentiment > 0.20, override the model's flat projection with an immediate upward step of 2-4 EUR.",
    "Adjust for post-spike overshoot: After a price spike, the model continues to forecast a slow recovery or plateau, whereas the true outcome often drops sharply or stabilizes at a lower level. Reduce long-horizon forecasts (days 20-30) by 3-5 EUR following any significant price spike to account for volatility decay."
  ]
}
